The Vela decision readout in converter.py adapts the mathematical forward pass in
vllm-sr/vela3-fast/vela3_encoder.py (Apache-2.0):
https://huggingface.co/vllm-sr/vela3-fast/blob/fa60e3aa41132c60bf05a84cabfdced39cb6d4f7/vela3_encoder.py

Changes: tensor inputs for marker positions and pooling, fixed-shape export,
and no upstream batching or task dispatch. The upstream license is reproduced
in licenses/vllm-sr-Apache-2.0.txt. Model weights are not included in this package.

Vela 3.1 complete conversion, 2026-11-17:
Original code and checkpoints: vllm-sr/vela3.1-fast, revision
0ed6ed301fbbf0c312f11a13ad17e3a6f8887262, Apache-2.0.
The complete upstream schema/decision heads, renderer, routing, LoRA operations
and decoding are retained. Core AI uses dynamic component graphs and original
FP32 weights in persistent state; no merging, quantization or retraining.
